  "authoringNote": "Migrated from F23; expectations re-derived under pack v2. The case states lcmpIncorporated true and the current usable final encounter states an incorporated LCMP report (evaluation 2026-08-18). Under C04 both R04 and R07 are manual_review, each with both held conditions: lcmp_stated_by_case (no document) and lcmp_stated_by_encounter naming f23-encounter v1, routed to the administrative reviewer with effect needs_human_review. The encounter is named in the condition only; parent sets are empty. Otherwise the pair is sequenced (encounter 2026-08-25, order 2026-09-08, same identifier), so no further R04 condition holds; C04 adds the LCMP conditions without suppressing any. R04 cites its six ordinary facts (LCMP fields are not R04 evidence); R07 cites the incorporated flag and the evaluation date. R01 passes: a stated LCMP incorporation is not a scope failure. R05 passes (receipt 2026-09-09 after the span). State needs_human_review, as in v1; v2 adds four condition tuples.",
